-- Help article for the Founder city badge (INSERT OR IGNORE, so an article edited in Admin is never overwritten). No prices here.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO help_articles (slug, title, category, kind, summary, body, keywords, video, sort, status, updated_by) VALUES ('founder-city-badge', 'What is the Founder city badge?', 'vote', 'answer', 'A small label on contests run by the first cities to use SoCal Lights. It does not affect votes or results, and it is not an endorsement.', 'You may see a small **Founder city** label on a contest page, in the contests list or on a results page. It marks contests run by one of the first cities to run contests on SoCal Lights.

## What it means
- The city is one of the first to run home decorating contests here, and is a founding partner. Founding partners also get one free contest, created by December 31, 2026.
- It shows only on that city''s own contests, and only while the badge is active (it can outlast the free contest).

## What it does not mean
- It does **not** change votes, judging, results, ranking or the order homes are listed in. Every home in every contest is treated the same way.
- It is **not** an endorsement. SoCal Lights does not say the city endorses it, and the label does not say SoCal Lights endorses the city.

Want to run a contest for your city? See [Start a contest](/add-contest).', 'founder city badge, founding partner, contest label, city contest', '', 90, 'published', 'seed');
